    "created_at": "2026-06-09T07:08:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-09T07:08:18Z",
    "body": "> In [w3c/navigation-timing#215 (comment)](https://github.com/w3c/navigation-timing/issues/215#issuecomment-4636746535) @achristensen07 suggests that we should also take the \"noreferrer\" values into account. This seems like we could add that condition here.\r\n\r\nThinking about this, I think it makes sense. We can think of it as:\r\n* The source navigation can opt-out of redirect timing (as it is the one choosing the redirectors) through `noreferrer`, or through Referrer-Policy.\r\n* The redirector itself can opt-in to timing through TAO, based on the destination origin",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
